    <string name="sgl_help_title">How to play Shooting Gallery</string>
    <string name="sgl_help_text">Tap the targets as they ride past. Your magazine holds six shots, then it reloads by itself (or press Reload early); shots while it reloads are wasted. A tin duck scores 10, or 25 for a small one. A ring target scores by zone: 10, 25 or 50 in the bullseye. A gold star scores 50 and refills your magazine. Never shoot the spiky decoy: it costs 30 points and breaks your combo. Hit targets in a row to build a combo, up to times four; a miss breaks it. Every player shoots the same range each round, so it is skill, not luck. Choose Relaxed pace for slower, larger targets, more time and a quicker reload. Pause stops the clock and hides the range.</string>
